# Service Architecture

## Service Layer Pattern
All business logic is encapsulated in service classes located in [src/services/](mdc:src/services). Each service handles a specific domain and integrates with external APIs or databases.

## Core Services

### Story Management
- **[story-service.ts](mdc:src/services/story-service.ts)**: CRUD operations for stories
- **[script-service.ts](mdc:src/services/script-service.ts)**: OpenAI integration for script generation

### Video Generation Pipeline
- **[tts-service.ts](mdc:src/services/tts-service.ts)**: OpenAI text-to-speech integration
- **[video-generation-service.ts](mdc:src/services/video-generation-service.ts)**: Runway ML API integration
- **[ffmpeg-service.ts](mdc:src/services/ffmpeg-service.ts)**: Video processing and assembly
- **[video-orchestration-service.ts](mdc:src/services/video-orchestration-service.ts)**: End-to-end pipeline coordination

## Service Patterns

### Error Handling
Each service has custom error classes:
```typescript
export class ServiceNameError extends Error {
  constructor(message: string, public code?: string) {
    super(message)
    this.name = 'ServiceNameError'
  }
}
```

### Singleton Pattern
Services are exported as singleton instances:
```typescript
export const serviceName = new ServiceNameClass()
```

### Database Integration
Services use [src/lib/supabase.ts](mdc:src/lib/supabase.ts) for database operations:
- Use `supabaseAdmin` for server-side operations
- Proper error handling for database failures
- Type-safe operations with TypeScript

### External API Integration
- **OpenAI**: Chat completions and TTS via `@ai-sdk/openai`
- **Runway ML**: Video generation via `@runwayml/sdk`


## Service Communication
- Services are consumed by **Server Actions** in [src/app/actions/](mdc:src/app/actions)
- Server Actions provide client-safe interfaces to services
- No direct service calls from client components
